1 NOTE {geni:about_me} "Rørdam and other historians, going back to Bartholins Cista Medica, claim that Søren Jessen was a councilman of Ribe, but his name does not apperar in the list of councilmen, nor in any of the Court proceedings su
2 CONC rviving from 1527-76. .. The surviving records of land ownership indicate that Severin Jessen owned a lot along the river, upon which some sort of structure was built. ("som hans brwhwss paa staar") in the 1540s and 1550s, but the
2 CONC re is no other mention of him." Schackelford 2004 p. 24 (footnote).
2 CONT
2 CONT Ribe, 1458  Originaltekst, Dansk Item Grawers Smeth hauer eth stykky jord aff byen, som ligger bagh i hans gardh, som schyller hwart aar 3 skilling lybsk som nw Jaspar Smeth haffuer som nw Unge Anders Kalissen oc Hans Pyskynd i wæ
2 CONC re haffuer szom nw '''Seuerinn Jessen''' i wære haffuer aff then iord, som hans brwhwss paa staar nw Mats Doordt Och nu Marrin mester Caspar Mulis Nu Niells Hansen, Hans Jessøns søns. [http://dendigitalebyport.byhistorie.dk/mediev
2 CONC al/item.aspx?itemid=1468]
2 CONT
2 CONT Fra den Seidelinske Slægtsbog citeres: SØREN JESSEN, Købmand i Ribe. Universitetsprogrammet over Sønnen PEDER SØRENSEN fortæller, at han var Raadmand, men han findes ikke paa Raadmandslisten i Kinchs »Ribe Bys Historie 1537-1660«.
2 CONC  Gift med BODIL SØRENSDATTER
