1 NAME Christian /Robson/
2 GIVN Christian
2 SURN Robson
2 _MARNM Robsahm
2 NICK Robsahm
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 3 JAN 1613
2 ADDR
3 STAE Scotland
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1678
2 PLAC Perhindersbo
2 ADDR
3 CITY Söderbärke
3 STAE Dalarnas län
3 POST 777 60
3 CTRY Sweden
1 OCCU Ryttare, Bruksägare å Malingsbo, Handelsman, Arrendator, Mallingsbo Gaard, Sødra Dalarne, inspektor, bruksdelägare, Bruksskrivare, Inspektor, delägare, köpman
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Christian Robson is the 7th great grandson of [https://www.geni.com/path/Robert-II-King-of-Scots+is+related+to+Christian-Robson?from=6000000000174222887&path_type=blood&to=6000000008393580620 Robert II, King of the
2 CONC  Scots]
2 CONT
2 CONT Primärkällor saknas för hans ursprung.
2 CONT Primary sources are missing for his origin.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Christian Robeson==
2 CONT b. 1587, Glasgow, , Lanark, Scotland  ????
2 CONT
2 CONT Inkom från Skottland till Sverige i slutet av 1500-talet (?), och skall ha givit sig ut som ryttare. Drev handel i Köping eller Västerås samt arrenderade Malingsbo Bruk i Söderbärke socken i Kopparbergs län och kallades av allmoge
2 CONC n för Malingsbo-tysken. Upptog Korslången, Nyfors och Nyhytte; fick i föräring därför en stor silverkanna död 1678 i Söderbärke socken vid pershindersbo. Hans porträtt målades då han var 63 år gammal, och ägdes sedemera av Abraham
2 CONC  Robsahm i Stockhom. Gift.
2 CONT
2 CONT [Ny Svensk Släktbok, 1906 sid. 493-504]
2 CONT
2 CONT Scottish Historical Review
2 CONT [Elgenstierna: Svenska Adelns Ättartavlor s. 377]
2 CONT
2 CONT One such branch was the family of Christian Robsahm. There are two lines of thought regarding
2 CONT the origin of the Robsahm surname. In the first theory, Robsahm is a Swedish variant of the Scottish
2 CONT names Robson/Robertson. As part of the Scottish connection, genealogists have assigned various
2 CONT parents to Christian Robsahm, without much supporting documentation: 1. He was the son of James
2 CONT Jacobsson Robeson and Joan Graham, born in Scotland and later moved to Sweden; and, 2. He was
2 CONT the son of Jacob Johansen Rubsaem and the grandson (some say son) of Jacob Robertson of Struan
2 CONT and Margarethe Blomen. Robertson himself moved to Sweden and became the personal physician
2 CONT of King Gustavus Adolphus. It is possible that Jacob Johansen Rubsaem was Christian's father, but of
2 CONT German descent, with no connection to Scotland. Supporting this, is the second theory of Christian's
2 CONT parentage, outlined in a 1920 book about Christian's son Lars, who moved to Norway in 1689. In
2 CONT the introduction it says: “The Robsahm's ancestor is known only by his Signet from 1587: JJR. Their
2 CONT heraldic shield includes a flowering turnip on a mountain.” The initials JJR could be Jacob Johansen
2 CONT Rubsaem. The syllable Rub in Rubsaem could be from rübe, the German word for turnip (Rapa or
2 CONT Rapum being the Latin name for Turnip), and the syllable saem could be from samen, the German
2 CONT word for seed. So Robsahm is possibly not connected to the Robertson/Robson clans of Scotland at
2 CONT all, but simply a homophone of Robson (some Rübsamen descendants in the USA have the surname,
2 CONT Turnipseed). Strengthening the argument is documentation that Christian was called by the Swedes
2 CONT "the Mallingsbo German", referring to his foundry at Mälingsbo in Dalarna County.
2 CONT Christian Robsahm was born about 1613 – 1615, probably in Germany, and grew up during the
2 CONT tumultuous Thirty Years’ War as it tore the Holy Roman Empire apart. Did the war influence
2 CONT Christian to move to Sweden? There’s no way to know for sure, but Sweden’s ruler Gustavus
2 CONT Adolphus was transforming his country to be more egalitarian, while also growing it militarily into
2 CONT a great power; a time known as Stormaktstiden ("The Great Power Era").
2 CONT In 1643 Christian met nineteen-year-old Catharina Christina Bertels, born in Klosterlausitz in
2 CONT the Duchy of Sachsen-Altenburg (suggesting that he too came from Saxony). They were married and
2 CONT moved to the county of Dalarna northwest of Stockholm. Christian worked as a trader in the towns
2 CONT of Köping and Västerås before being hired as a printer by the Kock-Cronström family, who were
2 CONT foundry owners in Dalarna. Christian began constructing hammers in the Kock-Cronström mills
2 CONT around Söderbärke parish, first at Klockarbo, then Larsbo. His experience eventually allowed him to
2 CONT lease a foundry, Mälingsbo Bruk. His final years were spent in Perhindersbo, just north of
2 CONT Söderbärke, where he lived out the remainder of his life.
2 CONT Source: Bill Chalk, T h e C h a l k F a m i l y H i s t o r y
2 CONT Part 3 — The Tjustman-Olson Families in Sweden, December 8, 2021 (Access via FamilySearch under Christian Robson profile/memories)
2 CONT -------------------
