1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *  Brockhoven:
2 CONT * Stavad "Mortensen". På latin "Buschovducensis".
2 CONT * Levde 1541 i Wittenberg, 
2 CONT * levde 1552 i Rostock, 
2 CONT * hovpräst hos Kristian III i Köpenhamn från 1552 till 1559, 
2 CONT * hovpräst hos hertig Magnus i Livland 1560.
2 CONT * Diakon och kanik vid Lunds domkyrka.
2 CONT * Föräldrar icke funna. Gravsten i Lunds domkyrka.
2 CONT * Källor: Isberg, A U: Malmö stads historia del I
2 CONT * Ekmans brev och anteckningar 1952 18/4, 1953 19/3. Dag Bremberg, Nils Bremberg
2 CONT
2 CONT German sources verify that he is the son of Nicholaas van Broeckhoven (name varies by country).  Was court pastor in Denmark, later at Lund Cathedral.    Educated at Wittenberg, and carried on a correspondence with Melancththon. R
2 CONC eferences to him can be found by searching Google Books.  For an online biography, see:    http://www.denstoredanske.dk/Dansk_Biografisk_Leksikon/Kirke_og_tro/Hofpr%C3%A6st/Henrik_v._Bruchofen 
2 CONT
2 CONT A number of articles that mention him can be found in Google books.  The name varies according to the language of the book cited.  
2 CONT
2 CONT An excellet source is found at http://books.google.com/books?id=alMAAAAAcAAJ&pg=PA195&dq=Buscoducensis&hl=en&sa=X&ei=YXR0UYPCJYWY2QXpoIDABw&ved=0CDIQ6AEwATgy  It includes the Latin inscription found at Lund Cathedral which mention
2 CONC s Anna, the second wife. 
2 CONT
2 CONT We are in the process of translating  Latin letters written from Melanchthon to Hendric Buscoducensis.    
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Hofpræst for Christian d. III. Canonikus i Lund.
2 CONT
2 CONT (Lb. Nr. 0/P768 1/2, side 455)
