1 NOTE Gjert was a student in 1648 and studied at the university in Copenhagen, then later at Wittenberg, and took the 'magister' (Ph.D.) degree in 1657.  In 1658 he retunded to Voss.  He had been away from home nine years.  He became cu
2 CONC rate to his father and also received the 'call' to succeed his father when he passed away in 1666.     Gjert Miltzow was both a literate and capable priest.  He wrote several books, among others one in Latin concerning the priests
2 CONC  in Voss and Hardanger. Gjert had inherited the good business sense of his family and bit by bit he aquired considerable property at Voss.  But he didn't forget the widows home his father had established.  In 1678 he gave the wido
2 CONC ws home considerable real estate.
