1 OCCU Kaptein i den dansk-norske marine / Overlos og innrulleringssjef i Stavanger
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Abo, Christian Nicolai,''' f. 1717; Søn af Underfoged og Arrestforvarer i Bergen; g. 1745 m. Anna Erlandsdatter Fieldberg, f. 1721, død 7/4 1812, Enke efter Kapellan Lars Werløe (Milit. Enkekasse Nr. 1063).<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT 13/9 1743 antaget til Maanedltnt. og beordret til Orlogsskibet ''Prinsesse Lovise'', 17/3 1744 Afsked, 27/5 1744 Sekltnt. og ansat ved Indrulleringen i Bergens Distrikt, 7/8 1755 tillagt Prltnt.s Kar. og Gage og flyttet til Indrul
2 CONC lering i Egersund; medens han er her, føres der af den franske Gesandt Ogier Klage over ham. Sagen skal undersøges (Adm. kgl. Res. 9/10 1760). Han havde paataget sig Kommission med nogle i Egersund indbragte Priser; dette paaanked
2 CONC e den franske Konsul i Bergen, Mr. Dechezaulz, da han mente, at alle burde henvende sig til ham i saadanne Sager. A. havde overtalt en til Konsulen bestemt Prise til at gaa ind til Egersund. En engelsk Kaper gik imidlertid efter o
2 CONC g tog den. Herover klagede saa Konsulen. Efter Undersøgelsen forflyttet til Indrullering i Mandal (Kgl. Res. 16/11 1760). 1761 m. Orlogsskibet ''Fyen'', 5/3 1763 beordret til Indrullering i Arendal, 23/12 1767 Kaptltnt., 9/1 1771 
2 CONC Indrulleringschef i Christianssands Distrikt, 27/12 1775 Kapt., 24/3 1777 Afsked som Indrulleringschef, 12/6 1778 Indrulleringsofficer i Stavanger (Kgl. Res.), 25/2 1784 forbigaaet ved Avancement, 6/3 1789 Indrulleringschef og Ove
2 CONC rlods i Stavanger Distrikt (Kgl. Res.), død 20/7 1789.<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT '''T. A. Topsøe-Jensen & Emil Marquard:''' ''Officerer i den Dansk-Norske Søetat 1660-1814 og den Danske Søetat 1814-1932'' (København 1935) Vol. I, p. 3.
1 FAMC @F6000000002898251185@
1 FAMS @F6000000019337251271@
1 FAMS @F6000000002898251177@
1 RFN geni:6000000002897997070
1 SUBM @S6000000000232888875@
1 NOTE      Christian Nicolai Abo, born Molde, Norway in the Diocese of Tronheim on 18th March 1718, was the son of a judge's assistant and gaoler in Bergen in Norway. In 1745 he married Anna Erlandsdatter Fieldberg (1721 to 1812) who wa
2 CONC s the widow of the curate Lars Werloe. Christian Nicolai spent his career with the Navy. In 1743 Christian Nicolai was employed as a "Monthly" Lieutenant on board the man-of-war "Princess Louise" and in 1744 he was employed as an 
2 CONC Enlist­ment Officer in the district of Bergen. In 1755 he was promoted to First Lieutenant and transferred to Egersund and then to Mandel. He remained with the Navy and by 1761 was on the man-of-war “Fyen”. In 1771 he was Chief of
2 CONC  Enlistment in the district of Christiansend and in 1778, the Enlistment Officer at Stavanger. He remained there for the rest of his life and in March 1789 he is recorded as the Chief of Enlistment and First Pilot in the district 
2 CONC of Stavanger. Presumably with 8 children he needed to remain employed because by this time he was 72 years old and in fact died on 20th July 1789 while still in service.
2 CONT
2 CONT The name shown in the Danish records is without the "von" or “van” which appears in the South African records. There is no evidence of its use in any of the Danish documents, including copies of letters signed by Töger Abo himself
2 CONC . It is possible that his son Christian Johannes adopted its use, when he arrived in South Africa years later.
