1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Christian Carstens,=
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Please see''' [https://www.geni.com/projects/Genealogia-Carstensia/40460 Genealogia Carsteniana]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.geni.com/people/Christian-Carstens/379921435660011045 '''Christian Carstens'''], born in Lübeck, Germany, moved to Denmark, and become the mayor of '''Tønder''', probably in 1566 (or died at that year). He is the ance
2 CONC stor of the Danish branch of the family Carstens. 
2 CONT
2 CONT His brother '''Frederik,''' again, is the ancestor of the Finnish branch of the family, or perhaps rather a son to Frederik, [https://www.geni.com/people/Henrik-Carstens/373073841810002408 '''Henrik Carstens'''] who also became a 
2 CONC Mayor, the first Mayor of '''Helsinki'''.  
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Christian Carstens===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Borgmester i Tønder''', f 1566. Han staar for Tiden som Slægtens Ældste. 1 Søn.
2 CONT
2 CONT /////
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Finnish and Danish''' branches of the Carstenses, finally, connected, bridge over Öresund built on Jan. 26th, 2020! by [https://www.geni.com/people/Mikko-Laakso/6000000035224749018 '''Dr. BDM''']. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The''' [https://dis-danmark.dk/bibliotek/909035.pdf '''link''' that verified] the connection, we owe to - always ever so nice curator - [https://www.geni.com/people/G%C3%BCnther-Kipp/5277343680110074074 Günther Kipp].  
2 CONT <br/>
2 CONT <br/>
