2 CONT http://www.danskeherregaarde.dk/manorholder/b/brejninggaard/ejerhistorie.aspx
2 CONT
2 CONT ◦Lange, Hans, 1542-1609, til Brejning og Kjærgaard, Søn af Gunde Lange til Brejning og Karen Breide, blev født paa Svendstrup 27. Maj 1542. Dronning Dorothea holdt ham og hans 2 Brødre i Skole sammen med sine egne Børn, og siden s
2 CONC tuderede han i København, Wittenberg, Strasburg og Paris. Efter sin Hjemkomst kom han 1563 i Kancelliet og deltog i den nordiske Syvaarskrig. Fra 1585-99 var han Lensmand paa Lundenæs. Han var en af de Adelsmænd, som 1589 ledsaged
2 CONC e Kongedatteren Elisabeth til Brunsvig. H. Lange, der havde prydet Brejning med en ny, anselig Hovedbygning, blev syg under Snapstinget i Viborg 1609 og døde paa Hjemrejsen paa Lysgaard i Hammerum Herred 2. Febr. Den 28. Aug. 1575
2 CONC  havde han ægtet Johanne Skram til Hersomgaard, Datter af Søhelten Peder S., og han havde med hende 10 Børn, deriblandt de her nævnte Sønner Gunde, Peder og Tyge Lange. Lange, Hans, 1542-1609, to Brejning and Kjærgaard, son of Gun
2 CONC de Lång til Brejning and Karen Breide, was born at Svendstrup on May 27, 1542. Queen Dorothea held him and his 2 brothers in school together with his own children, and since then he studied in Copenhagen, Wittenberg, Strasburg and
2 CONC  Paris. After his return, he arrived in the Chancellor in 1563 and participated in the Northern Sevens War. From 1585-99 he was a lender at Lundenæs. He was one of the noblemen who accompanied King Eight Elisabeth to Brunsvig in 1
2 CONC 589. H. Lange, who had embroidered Brejning with a new, majestic main building, became ill during the Snapsting in Viborg in 1609 and died on the journey at Lysgaard in Hammerum Herred 2. Feb. The 28th of August. In 1575 he had ma
2 CONC rried Johanne Skram to Hersomgaard, daughter of Søhelten Peder S. and he had 10 children including her sons, Geden, Peder and Tyge Lange.
