1 NOTE {geni:about_me} <strong>Wikipedia links: [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ole_R%C3%B8mer EN] | [https://da.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ole_R%C3%B8mer DA] | [https://no.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ole_Christensen_R%C3%B8mer NO] | [https://de.wikipedia
2 CONC .org/wiki/Ole_R%C3%B8mer DE] | [https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ole_Christensen_R%C3%B8mer FR]</strong>
2 CONT ==Wikipedia Biographical Summary:==
2 CONT {{https://s3.amazonaws.com/photos.geni.com/p13/29/33/19/5d/5344484a41859b31/ole_roemer_original.jpg|frame|left|300px}}
2 CONT
2 CONT "...'''Ole Christensen Rømer''' (25 September 1644, Århus – 19 September 1710, Copenhagen) was a Danish astronomer who in 1676 made <strong>the first quantitative measurements of the speed of light</strong>
2 CONT . In scientific literature alternative spellings such as "Roemer", "Römer", or "Romer" are common..."
2 CONT
2 CONT "...Rømer was born on 25 September 1644 in Århus to a merchant and skipper, Christen Pedersen, and Anna Olufsdatter Storm..."
2 CONT
2 CONT "...Rømer was employed by the French government: Louis XIV made him tutor for the Dauphin, and he also took part in the construction of the magnificent fountains at Versailles..."
2 CONT
2 CONT "...In 1681, Rømer returned to Denmark and was appointed professor of astronomy at the University of Copenhagen, and the same year he married Anne Marie Bartholin, the daughter of Rasmus Bartholin..."
2 CONT
2 CONT "...The Ole Rømer Museum is located in the municipality of Høje-Taastrup, Denmark..."
2 CONT
2 CONT >''SOURCE'': Wikipedia contributors, 'Ole Rømer', ''Wikipedia, The Free Encyclopedia'', 9 July 2011, 13:23 UTC, <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ole_R%C3%B8mer> [accessed 13 July 2011] 
