1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ely, Bendiderich, Stade 1713 Per Helge Seglsten  (View posts)	 Posted:	13 Apr 2000 1:00PM Classification: Query Surnames: Ely I am looking for information about my ancestor Bendiderich (von) Ely, who was leutenant 
2 CONC wachtmeister and kapitän wachtmeister in the danish army in Stade between 1713 and 1715. He might have remained in stade after Denmark abandoned the area, or he might have gone to Oldenburg which remained danish until the 1770s. B
2 CONC endiderich was probably in his late 60s when he came to Stade, and has probably died in the Stade-area or in Oldenburg. Any hints on where I might find clues to what happened to Bendiderich will be greatly appreciated.
2 CONT
2 CONT Regards Per Helge Seglsten Oslo, Norway
