1 CONT Margaret of Denmark (June 23, 1456 - before July 14, 1486) was thedaughter of King Christian I of Denmark (1448-81), Norway (1450-81),and Sweden (1457-64), and his wife Dorothea of Brandenburg.
1 CONT
1 CONT In July, 1469, at Holyrood Abbey, she married James III Stuart, theKing of Scotland (1460-88).
1 CONT
1 CONT This marriage produced three sons :
1 CONT
1 CONT James IV (March 17, 1473 - September 9, 1513)
1 CONT James Stewart, Duke of Ross (March 1476 - January 1504), and
1 CONT John Stewart, Earl of Mar (December 1479 - 1503).
1 CONT She died at Stirling Castle and is buried in Cambuskenneth Abbey.
